  "project_id": 7898047,
  "title": "wlan: fix wrong reported length for reassembled payloads",
  "description": "There is no need to remove the FCS at the end of the reassembled payload since FCS bytes have already been removed from the fragments. Also, the way it was removed in the code was wrong: it set the reported length of the reassembled payload to the reported length of the last fragment only.\n\nIt might also make sense to use `next_tvb` instead of `tvb` in the call to `process_reassembled_data()` at line [26877](https://gitlab.com/wireshark/wireshark/-/merge_requests/1178/diffs#17db83fabbbb3bb40cb8fa5ffd0d1a14b2a2cfb3_26877_26877).",
