    {
      "id": "1b77bac0086d59e1f9855f490628f71b3be562b9",
      "individual_note": true,
      "resolvable": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 463472395,
          "type": null,
          "body": "Attached file [defrag_bug-redacted.pcap](/uploads/9bc00440d2a71d9e2123deefc5faa156/defrag_bug-redacted.pcap) show the problems that occur because reassembled frame length is truncated when FCS is present in frames. We can also clearly observe that no FCS is ever part of the reassembled frames.\n\nAfter removing the code lines as this MR does, there is no more issue.\n\nMAC addresses have been redacted in the pcap file, so FCS fields are wrong, but this is unrelated to the issue this MR fixes.",
